# Spring Boot Local Properties
#
# The bare pattern keeps a developer's personal overrides out of the repository.
# It must not swallow the tracked local runtime contract: modules ship
# src/main/resources/application-local.yml as the profile that lets them start
# standalone, and tests assert its contents.
#
# Without the negations below the file is ignored silently — `git add` reports
# nothing and the commit lands without it, leaving tests that reference the
# profile red. That is how loan/batch and journal-ledger/api ended up with no
# local profile, and why several already-tracked files exist only because
# someone happened to run `git add -f`.
#
# Keep all three spellings symmetric. Previously only .yml was listed, so
# application-local.yaml was never ignored anywhere — the modules using that
# spelling committed theirs without noticing, which is what made the gap look
# arbitrary. Anything outside src/{main,test}/resources stays ignored.
#
# Note the .properties rows change behaviour rather than just restoring it:
# that spelling was ignored everywhere before, including under
# src/{main,test}/resources, and is now trackable there. No module ships one
# today, so this only opens the door for a future one to be committed the same
# way as its .yml/.yaml siblings.
application-local.properties
application-local.yml
application-local.yaml
!**/src/main/resources/application-local.properties
!**/src/main/resources/application-local.yml
!**/src/main/resources/application-local.yaml
!**/src/test/resources/application-local.properties
!**/src/test/resources/application-local.yml
!**/src/test/resources/application-local.yaml

# Hexagonal Architecture Exception
# Keep source packages named "port/out" or "adapter/out" (don't ignore them if they are in src)
!**/src/main/java/**/port/out/
!**/src/main/java/**/port/out/*.java
!**/src/main/java/**/adapter/out/
!**/src/main/java/**/adapter/out/**
!**/src/test/java/**/adapter/out/
!**/src/test/java/**/adapter/out/**
